On Wed, Jun 3, 2009 at 12:38 PM, tijlan <jbotijlan@gmail.com> wrote:
> Wouldn't it be cool if we
> could do the following ("pe'ei" being an experimental, inversive
> version of "pe"):
>
>  la .ken. pe'ei lo verba pe'ei lo plise cu gunro

If "pe'ei" is in selmaho GOI, the grouping is "la .ken. pe'ei (lo
verba pe'ei lo plise)", so you would need  "la .ken. pe'ei lo verba
ge'u pe'ei lo plise" to get the right grouping.

We could also use "se pe" instead of "pe'ei", that way we don't need
to add new words for the reverse of "po" and "po'e" as well, just a
minor adjustment of the grammar.

